The open-loop transfer function is \[G(s)=\frac{150}{s(s+9)(s+25)}\] The phase angle is \[\angle G(j\omega)=-90^\circ-\tan^{-1}\!\left(\frac{\omega}{9}\right)-\tan^{-1}\!\left(\frac{\omega}{25}\right)\] At the phase crossover frequency, \(\angle G(j\omega_{pc})=-180^\circ.\) \[\tan^{-1}\!\left(\frac{\omega_{pc}}{9}\right)+
\tan^{-1}\!\left(\frac{\omega_{pc}}{25}\right)=90^\circ\] Using \(\tan^{-1}x+\tan^{-1}y=90^\circ
\quad\Rightarrow\quad
xy=1,\) we get \[\frac{\omega_{pc}}{9}\times\frac{\omega_{pc}}{25}=1\] \[\omega_{pc}=15\ \text{rad/s}\] The magnitude at the phase crossover frequency is \[|G(j15)|
=\frac{150}{15\sqrt{15^2+9^2}\sqrt{15^2+25^2}}
=\frac{150}{15\sqrt{306}\sqrt{850}}
=0.01974\] Hence, \[\text{GM}=\frac{1}{|G(j15)|}=50.65\] \[\text{GM}_{\mathrm{dB}}
=20\log_{10}(50.65)
=34.1\ \text{dB}\] \[\boxed{(C)\;34.1~\text{dB}}\]

